Subject: SUMMARY: Adding disks in LSM to DU40b
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078612210716

My thanks to Alan from Digital Support (Atlanta):

According to Alan, the problem is related to the SCSI bus
holding the devices which is preventing LSM on systemB (DU40b)
from accessing them.

His solution:

from systemA (du32c) - voldg deport test_dg
                       voldisk rm rz18
                       scu -f /dev/rrz18c release device

from systemB (du40b) - voldisk define rz18
                       voldg import test_dg
                       volume start test_vol
                       volprint -Aht (to check)
                       You may need to make the soft link if using Advfs
                       in /etc/fdmns.

It worked!

Thanks again Alan.

Les Mayeda
mayeda@csmc.edu




