---------- Forwarded message ----------

The original question was "why advfsd is using more than 90% of the cpu?"

It's a known bug and there is no correction available but just workarounds.
The daemon is useful only with the advfs GUI.

2 solutions are given :

1) On a regular basis stop and start the daemon by :

/sbin/rc3.d/S53advfsd stop
/sbin/rc3.d/S53advfsd start

2) stop the daemon by /sbin/rc3.d/S53advfsd stop and start it only before 
using the GUI.

Daniel


