From tru64-unix-managers  Thu May 22 13:35:06 1997
From: GRANDLE () acodbob ! larc ! nasa ! gov
Date: Thu, 22 May 1997 13:35:06 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: sumary of vxt2000 reset to factory defaults problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078612210549

Thanks to all who replied.

The method of reseting the VXT2000 to the factory defaults is
as followd

1. get the machine to the boot state ie. >>> on the screen
  do this by pressing the halt button on the back just
  under the network interface connectors.  If the machine
  has been set to autoboot mode, then disconnect the
  network and it will fail the network test and drop into
  the boot mode.

2. at the >>> prompt type
   T/UTIL 1

   This will reset to the factory defaults(  it does work)

3. reboot the machine with
   B/10000 

   ( if you disconnected the network in step 1 reconnect
     before booting).
   The /10000 clears the stored boot record sequence as
   that it will try all boots methods. Don't
   know of the T/UTIL 1 does this as well as I did not
   try the standard boot first.)


Bob Grandle

