Greetings - 

For those of you whom have downloaded sys_stat-x.y, I
have updated it to version 1.6.  Sys_stat-1.6 includes
user, swap, and UBC high and low water marks in the 
display and the log file.  If you are running V4.0+
of Digital UNIX, the sys_stat interactive display
also shows the average millisecond per transfer for
your disks.  

For those of you interested in the VM subsystem of
Digital UNIX, I have an additional utility called
vm_mon which displays real-time VM subsystem data.
In the initial version (v1.0), there is precious
little documentation for what's displayed (actually
none), but it's a start.

I have also included a utility to show disk I/O
performance from Digital UNIX v4.0+ systems.

All of these utilities may be found at my usual
location:  ftp://raven.alaska.edu/pub/randy
in the directory perf_mon_tools.

The utilities are called sys_stat-1.6.tar.gz,
vm_mon-1.0.tar.gz, and disks-1.0.tar.gz respectively.

As usual, send comments, bug reports, etc... to me
at haymanr@icefog.alaska.edu.


