From tru64-unix-managers  Wed May 21 13:16:24 1997
From: "Daniel A. Monjar" <dmonjar () worldnet ! att ! net>
Date: Wed, 21 May 1997 13:16:24 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: help with an RZ28
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078612210507

problem synopsis:
+++
I have a spare RZ29b that I want to put in my PC.  I have an Adaptec ISA to
Fast-SCSI adapter that see the drive and identifies it as a DEC RZ29b
device and puts it on drive D:.  But when I use the adapter bios to perform
media scanning of the drive it immediately reports back an error.  Did DEC
does something to the drives to make it more/less than a Seagate Barracuda?
 Is my quest to use this drive on my PC doomed to fail?  Or is the drive
dead?
---

Answer:  DEC changes these drives to not spin up by default but to require
the START UNIT command from the controller.  I can change a jumper setting
to make the drive spin at power up.  There was also a discussion of drive
sector lengths and the fact that the Adaptec's don't like non-512 sectors


thanks to:
Paul Bunn, BEI
Ross Alexander
Paul Kitwin
John Francini
David A. Nicholson
Hernando Barragan
Martyn Johnson

