I'd like to thank the following for thier responses:

rwa@cs.athabascau.ca
aad@nwnet.net
ckrieger@latrade.com
rajeshkapoor@hotmail.com
dedera@valm.sk
serge.collin@electrabel.be


The question:  I have an Alphaserver 1000/266 running 3.2d.  It
currently has a DE-435 10Mb card, and I want to add a DE500 card.  
After installing the card and booting, I did not see the card
on netstat -in

The soloution:

A new kernel needed to be built.  The "quick" steps to this are:

1) Add the network interface to /usr/sys/conf/MACHINENAME, with 
corresponding PCI slot information.

2) Boot with the generic kernel, genvmunix

3) Run a "doconfig -c MACHINENAME"

4) After the kernel is built, copy /sys/MACHINENAME/vmunix to /

5) Reboot, and the interface appears.

6) Configure the card

A word of caution, make sure to copy your old kernel and config file 
before modifying anything , just in case you need to go back.


David

