From tru64-unix-managers  Fri May 02 10:07:50 1997
From: "Eric Wyn Jones (01248-382407)" <e.w.jones () bangor ! ac ! uk>
Date: Fri, 02 May 1997 10:07:50 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Comments in /etc/printcap and a moan about print filters
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078612210126


I asked :-

Anybody know if you can have comments between continuation lines
in a printcap entry ?

Robert Evans <r.evans@ic.ac.uk>,Peter Stern <peter@wiscpa.weizmann.ac.il>,
John Stoffel <jfs@fluent.com>  and rrens@hcia.com 

all gave the correct answer i.e. NO
They pointed out that continuation lines are equivalent to one long line 
- so the line would not be starting with a # sign.

Now they need to tell the people that write the configuration utility for
the Rapidprint200 (a printer N.I.C.) because it generates this sort of
thing :-

# 
# This printcap entry is automatically generated for the N.I.C. product 
# Simple input and output filters are provided for your convenience. 
eroc|N.I.C. printer :\ 
        :lp=/dev/nic_2/eroc:\ 
        :if=/usr/nic_2/infilter:\ 
#       :of=/usr/nic_2/outfilter:\ 
        :sd=/usr/spool/eroc: 
#


Thanks also to :-
  "Jude T. Cruz" <jude@tsi.com.my>
for a suggestion to up and down the printer between edits to printcap -
not applicable in this case !


