Subject: VXT-2000+ Blues
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078612210271

To make the VXT2000 usable with packages like Netscape
 you need to load it from an Infoserver (e.g. Infoserver 1000)
 which allows virtual memory expansion via paging files. The
 crashing problem arises because the VXT load host software
 doesn't support paging files (as far as I know anyway).

You may be able to use Netscape for a while if you have
 the full VX2000 memory configuration but sooner or later
 you'll open one window too many ... 

DIGITAL are manufacturing  the Infoserver 1000 again (probably
 because of the above problems!).

Good luck,
 John
